### Customer API demonstration
### Prerequisites: application running on http://localhost:8080
### In IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client, run requests top-to-bottom.
### The create response id is captured into @customerId for later requests.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@customerId = {{createCustomer.response.body.id}}

### 1. Create a customer
# @name createCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ada",
  "lastName": "Lovelace",
  "email": "ada.lovelace@example.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 2. Retrieve the created customer by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}

### 3. List all customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers

### 4. Update the customer
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Augusta Ada",
  "lastName": "Lovelace",
  "email": "ada.lovelace@example.com",
  "status": "INACTIVE"
}

### 5. Retrieve the updated customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}

### 6. Delete the customer
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}

### 7. Attempt to retrieve a deleted customer (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}

### 8. Validation error — blank firstName (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": " ",
  "lastName": "Hopper",
  "email": "grace.hopper@example.com",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### Optional: duplicate email conflict (expect 409)
# Create once, then run again with the same email.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Grace",
  "lastName": "Hopper",
  "email": "grace.hopper@example.com",
  "status": "PENDING"
}
